{
  "title": "Arcos, Spain",
  "indexDescription": "Our stay at Arcos de la Frontera Spain in 2009.",
  "description": "We drove our small rental van from Málaga to Arcos de la Frontera Spain and parked in the flat land in the new part of town since there was little parking by our place.  We walked the narrow streets and steps up the hill to our rooms.  Our hosts were a friendly couple from England.  The first night we ate at a cave like restaurant in the historical district on a side hill with rock arches and walls and it must have been 600 years old.  They severed blood sausages.\n\nWe stayed a couple of days.  Kathleen was proud when the checkout clerk at the grocery store thought she was French.\n\nIt rained like crazy.  We bought five umbrellas, however with the wind and rain they only lasted a couple of days.",
  "cNum": 52,
  "posted": "2026-10-21",
  "location": "36.7487889, -5.8060994",
